From: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fan: don't report a startup race as a missing config

createSensors() runs from a GetSensorConfiguration callback that fires
again on every InterfacesAdded. On a cold boot it therefore runs once
before entity-manager has published any board configuration at all, and
with nothing to match against, every fan found in sysfs reports

    failed to find match for '/sys/class/hwmon/hwmon0/fan1_input'

before matching correctly seconds later once the configuration arrives.
On this board that is three error lines per boot for three fans that are
configured perfectly well.

Distinguish the two cases by the only thing that separates them: whether
there were any configurations to match against. An unmatched fan with a
populated configuration set is still a real misconfiguration and is
still logged at error.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/src/fan/FanMain.cpp b/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
index 8b20d20a5..65a650347 100644
--- a/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
+++ b/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
@@ -410,8 +410,24 @@ void createSensors(
             }
             if (sensorData == nullptr)
             {
-                lg2::error("failed to find match for '{PATH}'", "PATH",
-                           path.string());
+                // This callback re-runs on every InterfacesAdded, so on a cold
+                // boot it fires once before entity-manager has published any
+                // board configuration at all. With nothing to match against,
+                // every fan in sysfs "fails to find a match" and then matches
+                // fine seconds later -- a startup race, not a misconfigured
+                // system. Only complain once there are configurations to have
+                // matched against.
+                if (sensorConfigurations.empty())
+                {
+                    lg2::debug(
+                        "no configurations loaded yet, deferring '{PATH}'",
+                        "PATH", path.string());
+                }
+                else
+                {
+                    lg2::error("failed to find match for '{PATH}'", "PATH",
+                               path.string());
+                }
                 continue;
             }
 
